  "details": "It seems that proper validation is not done when reading from Avatar parameter storage.\n\nUsers can set any value for Avatar Height up to the hard limit without Udon.\n\nreproduction steps\n\n1. Select an avatar that is not cached in the currently running VRChat as the target for scale change.\n\n2. Enter a large value in the \"eyeHeight\" key that exists in the JSON with the same name as the avatar ID.\n\n3. When I change to the target avatar, I can see that the stored value is used as the avatar's height.\n\n4. The avatar appears to others to be over 5 meters tall.",
